%description:

Tcp.mss:auto-ipv6 -- with -1, an IPv6 host announces the MSS of an MTU of 1500 bytes.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "-1: the MSS of the address family for an MTU of 1500 bytes, 1460 for
IPv4 and 1440 for IPv6, when the peer is known".

The classes: auto (-1, the default), with a facet for IPv4 and one for IPv6; explicit (88 and
more); invalid (0 to 87, and below -1). The code: TcpConnection::initConnection() and
resolveAddressFamilyMss(). This test separates "auto" from "explicit".

Host under test: host1, the active opener, on IPv6; it opens at 3 s, after Duplicate Address
Detection. Observation: level 1, the MSS option of the SYN of host1 is 1440.

%# parameter: Tcp.mss
%# class: auto-ipv6
%# value: -1
%# key: *.host1.tcp.mss
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpMssAutoIpv6")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) { return tcpMssOptionOf(context.event.packet) == 1440; })
                  .describe("the SYN of host1, with the MSS 1440")
                  .within(4.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpMssAutoIpv6 compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.mss = -1    # the parameter under test
*.host*.typename = "StandardHost6"
*.configurator.typename = "Ipv6FlatNetworkConfigurator"
*.host1.app[0].tOpen = 3s
*.host1.app[0].tSend = 3.1s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpMssAutoIpv6: PASS
